  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "At Qin Bai Sheng’s auction, bidders discuss a sandalwood sacred elephant egg offered alongside Immortal Gu. A sandalwood sacred elephant is an ancient desolate beast; after it grows to adulthood, it can rival rank seven Gu Immortals. Onlookers say a living ancient desolate beast managed well is like a treasure trove with endless value, and that the blood of the sacred elephant is a good immortal material. In the same auction talk, regenerating tusks are named beside that blood yield; those harvests are covered on sacred elephant tusks and sandalwood sacred elephant egg.",
      "chapters": [
        754
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "living-beast-yield",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_qin_bai_sheng",
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "res_sacred_elephant_tusks",
        "res_sandalwood_sacred_elephant_egg"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In a giant space-path Gu formation, Fang Yuan finds three sandalwood sacred elephant corpses among other desolate and ancient desolate beast remains. Sandalwood sacred elephants are rare across the five regions and barely seen, and a mature one has rank seven Gu Immortal battle strength. Narration recalls the earlier Qin Bai Sheng auction bid that used a sandalwood sacred elephant egg and drew a huge commotion.",
      "chapters": [
        935
      ],
